1
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:29,320
Good evening. Our lead story.

2
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:34,159
ENCOM CEO and video game icon 
Kevin Flynn has disappeared.

3
00:00:34,242 --> 00:00:37,287
He was best known for designing Tron 
and Space Paranoids,

4
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:40,123
the two bestselling video games 
in history.

5
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:43,376
Flynn took ownership of ENCOM 
in 1982

6
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:46,838
as the company skyrocketed 
to the top of the tech industry.

7
00:00:46,921 --> 00:00:51,217
But things changed in 1985 
with the untimely death of Flynn's wife,

8
00:00:51,342 --> 00:00:53,845
the mother of his young son, Sam.

9
00:00:53,928 --> 00:00:55,930
Recently, ENCOM board members

10
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:57,223
have been troubled by reports

11
00:00:57,348 --> 00:01:00,310
of Flynn's erratic, 
even obsessive, behavior.

12
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:04,105
With Flynn missing, 
the company is now in chaos.

13
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:06,399
This afternoon, ENCOM's board

14
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:09,694
moved to seize control 
from Flynn's partner, Alan Bradley,

15
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:12,781
vowing to return the company 
to profitability.

16
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:18,077
Loyal to the end, Bradley maintains 
his belief that Flynn is not missing

17
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:20,747
and is instead pursuing his dream of

18
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:24,292
"a digital frontier 
to reshape the human condition."

19
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:06,394
Now that is a big door.

20
00:03:06,477 --> 00:03:07,770
Welcome, everybody.

21
00:03:08,146 --> 00:03:11,399
Please settle. I know it's late, 
so I'll skip the pleasantries

22
00:03:11,482 --> 00:03:15,195
and hand things over to our chairman, 
Richard Mackey.

23
00:03:17,363 --> 00:03:20,116
Thank you. Thank you. 
Thank you, Claire.

24
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:23,786
Tonight I am pleased to announce

25
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:29,834
that ENCOM's last fiscal year 
was our most profitable ever.

26
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:31,794
Yes.

27
00:03:50,521 --> 00:03:53,942
At midnight the 1 2th version 
of our flagship operating system

28
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:56,402
will hit the shelves around the world.

29
00:03:57,862 --> 00:04:00,281
I'm sure it comes as no surprise 
whom we have to thank.

30
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:02,450
The head of our software design team,

31
00:04:02,533 --> 00:04:07,497
a man whose father's 
own notable history with ENCOM

32
00:04:07,622 --> 00:04:10,333
helped make this company 
what it is today.

33
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:15,380
Edward Dillinger. Well done.

34
00:04:15,797 --> 00:04:17,257
Well done.

35
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:25,223
And this year, simultaneous 
to the release of ENCOM OS-12,

36
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:31,312
we will be making our debut 
on Tokyo's Nikkei Index.

37
00:04:31,437 --> 00:04:36,317
ENCOM's stock will now trade 
around the world 2 4l7.

38
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:38,945
Huh? Oh, yes.

39
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:05,555
- Excuse me. 
- Yes, Alan?

40
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:07,140
Given the prices

41
00:05:07,265 --> 00:05:10,893
that we charge to students and schools,

42
00:05:11,894 --> 00:05:14,564
what sort of improvements 
have been made in Flynn...

43
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:18,318
I mean, ENCOM OS-12?

44
00:05:21,487 --> 00:05:24,866
This year we put a "12" on the box.

45
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:29,245
OS-12 is the most secure 
operating system ever released.

46
00:05:30,204 --> 00:05:34,000
The idea of sharing our software 
or giving it away for free

47
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:36,919
disappeared with Kevin Flynn.

48
00:05:50,641 --> 00:05:52,602
I know you're here.

49
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:55,104
Let's make this easy.

50
00:05:57,982 --> 00:05:59,108
Come on, come on.

51
00:06:07,575 --> 00:06:08,826
Freeze!

52
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:10,661
Okay.

53
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:12,497
If there are no more questions,

54
00:06:13,081 --> 00:06:16,125
I would like you to meet 
our next blockbuster.

55
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:18,961
ENCOM OS-12.

56
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:22,256
Whoa.

57
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,634
Still a few bugs.

58
00:06:24,759 --> 00:06:26,385
What's that? What is that?

59
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:32,475
Just bear with us one sec.

60
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,727
Make this go away now.

61
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:38,981
...where ENCOM's chairman, 
Richard Mackey, will be launching...

62
00:06:39,107 --> 00:06:42,443
- We go live in 30 seconds. 
- He's on the roof!

63
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:45,321
- Anyone know where the master file is? 
- I do.

64
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,074
It's on the Web.

65
00:06:50,326 --> 00:06:51,994
We've got to stop this.

66
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:58,334
I've got to ring that opening bell.

67
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:01,045
- Make this stop now. 
- It's locked.

68
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:04,048
Just shut it down. Shut it down! Now!

69
00:07:04,173 --> 00:07:07,135
Relax, Mackey. Relax.

70
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:08,553
It's under control.

71
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:10,680
Relax? Our most valuable

72
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:14,308
and most secure operating system 
is out there for free!

73
00:07:14,433 --> 00:07:16,102
How am I supposed to explain that?

74
00:07:16,185 --> 00:07:19,147
I don't know. 
Say it was all part of the plan.

75
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:22,316
A little gift from ENCOM.

76
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:26,487
Apparently, ENCOM Technology 
is having some technical difficulties.

77
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:30,992
Why don't we give them a chance 
to sort things out?

78
00:07:58,102 --> 00:08:00,062
Hey, Dad.

79
00:08:00,229 --> 00:08:01,981
How you doing?

80
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:11,657
- Where you gonna run to now? 
- Hey, you don't wanna do that.

81
00:08:11,741 --> 00:08:14,035
Didn't anyone tell you? 
Stealing is wrong.

82
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,746
You can't steal 
what was designed to be free.

83
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:19,999
- Now I got you. 
- Your boss is okay with this.

84
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:21,375
The hell he is.

85
00:08:21,834 --> 00:08:23,586
Your boss works for the CEO

86
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:25,296
and the CEO 
works for the shareholders.

87
00:08:25,421 --> 00:08:27,715
Do you know 
who the biggest shareholder is?

88
00:08:28,716 --> 00:08:30,301
I don't know. Some kid.

89
00:08:34,555 --> 00:08:36,224
You're Mr. Flynn?

90
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:39,602
Why?

91
00:08:40,269 --> 00:08:42,605
This is your father's company.

92
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:46,234
- Not anymore. 
- What? Hey. Hey, kid.

93
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:48,986
No!

94
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:02,124
Yeah.

95
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:04,919
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

96
00:09:09,465 --> 00:09:10,675
You kidding me?

97
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:15,388
- That's him! Get the team down here! 
- There he is! Get him!

98
00:09:17,056 --> 00:09:18,558
What the...

99
00:09:18,849 --> 00:09:20,977
Hey! No free ride!

100
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:24,146
- Whoa! 
- No free taxi!

101
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:26,148
You pay!

102
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:31,362
- Whoa, whoa, whoa! 
- No free ride!

103
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:44,000
Hold it right there. Freeze!

104
00:09:45,918 --> 00:09:49,297
Okay, boys. You got me.

105
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:51,215
Hey.

106
00:10:56,864 --> 00:10:58,949
- Hey, Karl. 
- Hey, how you doing?

107
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:17,301
Enjoy it, Marv. You earned it.

108
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:23,140
Why are you in my apartment, Alan?

109
00:11:26,561 --> 00:11:28,479
- How you been, Sam? 
- Oh, you know,

110
00:11:28,604 --> 00:11:32,233
when I was 12, I appreciated 
the surrogate-father thing. But come on.

111
00:11:33,026 --> 00:11:34,902
I got it all under control now.

112
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,405
Oh. Clearly!

113
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:38,740
You want to help me 
with my homework?

114
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:40,283
Like old times? Have a catch?

115
00:11:42,702 --> 00:11:46,164
You know, 
you got a pretty nice view here.

116
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:52,128
Heard you did a triple axel off of her 
a few hours ago.

117
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:56,007
- Rough landing, huh? 
- Could have been worse.

118
00:11:56,132 --> 00:11:58,926
I also thought your message 
to the board

119
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:00,136
was very clever.

120
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:02,722
Did you like that? That was Marv's idea.

121
00:12:08,394 --> 00:12:11,147
Alan, are we really 
going to do this again?

122
00:12:12,023 --> 00:12:15,109
Do I really look like I'm ready 
to run a Fortune 500 company?

123
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:16,861
No.

124
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:21,199
And truthfully, the company 
is pretty happy with where you are, too.

125
00:12:21,616 --> 00:12:22,575
I bet.

126
00:12:22,742 --> 00:12:25,870
That way they can keep doing 
whatever they want.

127
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:32,001
You know, I guess what I find curious 
is the crazy charities,

128
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:34,545
the annual prank on the company.

129
00:12:34,962 --> 00:12:37,507
You have an interesting way 
of being disinterested, Sam.

130
00:12:37,632 --> 00:12:39,425
Why are you here, Alan?

131
00:12:42,804 --> 00:12:44,472
I was paged last night.

132
00:12:44,639 --> 00:12:46,808
Oh, man, still rocking the pager?

133
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:48,518
Good for you.

134
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:53,022
Yeah, your dad once told me 
I had to sleep with it, and I still do.

135
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:56,484
Page came from your dad's office 
at the arcade.

136
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:02,657
- So? 
- So?

137
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:06,452
That number's been disconnected 
for 20 years.

138
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:11,416
Sam, two nights before he disappeared, 
he came to my house.

139
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:14,168
"I've cracked it," he kept saying.

140
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:18,047
He was talking about genetic 
algorithms, quantum teleportation.

141
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:22,427
He said he was about to change 
everything. Science, medicine, religion.

142
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:26,013
He wouldn't have left that, Sam.

143
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:30,435
He wouldn't have left you.

144
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:34,188
Oh, Alan. You're the only one 
who still believes that.

145
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:37,358
He's either dead 
or chilling in Costa Rica.

146
00:13:38,401 --> 00:13:39,986
Probably both.

147
00:13:40,737 --> 00:13:42,196
Look, I'm sorry.

148
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:44,782
I'm tired, and I smell like jail.

149
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:49,829
Let's just reconvene in another couple 
of years, huh? What do you say?

150
00:13:53,875 --> 00:13:55,042
Here.

151
00:13:56,252 --> 00:13:58,629
These are the keys to the arcade.

152
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:04,510
I haven't gone over there yet. 
I thought you should be the one.

153
00:14:04,594 --> 00:14:07,972
Alan, you're acting like I'm gonna 
find him sitting there working.

154
00:14:08,139 --> 00:14:11,893
Just, "Hey, kiddo. Lost track of time."

155
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:17,565
Wouldn't that be something?

156
00:14:25,823 --> 00:14:28,367
What?

157
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:45,982
You son of a gun.

158
00:18:26,856 --> 00:18:28,357
Flynn.

159
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:35,573
Huh.

160
00:18:36,782 --> 00:18:38,701
Let's try the back door.

161
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:44,165
What were you working on?

162
00:18:51,046 --> 00:18:52,673
LaserControl.

163
00:18:53,507 --> 00:18:54,884
Okay.

164
00:19:35,466 --> 00:19:37,551
This isn't happening.

165
00:19:53,359 --> 00:19:55,236
Oh, man, this is happening.

166
00:20:04,411 --> 00:20:05,746
Wait.

167
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:09,416
This program has no disk. 
Another stray.

168
00:20:09,542 --> 00:20:10,543
Hey, wait.

169
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:13,379
Wait. I'm not a program!

170
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:44,285
He actually did it.

171
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:49,456
I'm on the Grid.

172
00:20:59,091 --> 00:21:02,428
Does the name Kevin Flynn 
mean anything to you?

173
00:21:02,511 --> 00:21:04,430
Be quiet if you want to live!

174
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:06,765
Not the games, not the games,

175
00:21:06,849 --> 00:21:09,268
not the games, not the games...

176
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:10,686
What's his problem?

177
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:15,482
Not the games, not the...

178
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:04,448
Rectify.

179
00:22:07,785 --> 00:22:09,370
Rectify.

180
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:15,793
- Games. 
- No. Please!

181
00:22:15,918 --> 00:22:16,961
Rectify.

182
00:22:17,086 --> 00:22:20,089
You probably get this a lot, 
but there's been a big mistake.

183
00:22:20,172 --> 00:22:21,882
Games.

184
00:22:21,882 --> 00:22:23,676
- Please, no, no. 
- Whoa. Hey.

185
00:23:04,967 --> 00:23:07,970
Er, can somebody tell me what the...

186
00:23:12,599 --> 00:23:14,810
Hey, hey. It's got a zipper.

187
00:23:32,453 --> 00:23:33,912
He is different.

188
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:43,881
This can't be good.

189
00:23:53,724 --> 00:23:58,645
Attention, program. 
You will receive an identity disk.

190
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:04,360
Everything you do or learn 
will be imprinted on this disk.

191
00:24:05,402 --> 00:24:09,323
If you lose your disk 
or fail to follow commands,

192
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:13,243
you will be subject 
to immediate de-resolution.

193
00:24:19,458 --> 00:24:22,711
Mirroring complete. 
Disk activated and synchronized.

194
00:24:22,961 --> 00:24:24,254
Proceed to games.

195
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:27,716
Games?

196
00:24:31,595 --> 00:24:33,222
Where are you going?

197
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:41,563
What am I supposed to do?

198
00:24:42,606 --> 00:24:44,399
Survive.

199
00:25:36,535 --> 00:25:40,205
All combatants, 
prepare for disk wars.

200
00:25:40,330 --> 00:25:43,792
Disk wars! Disk wars!

201
00:25:44,751 --> 00:25:46,044
Disk wars!

202
00:25:47,171 --> 00:25:48,672
Disk wars!

203
00:25:49,965 --> 00:25:51,925
Disk wars!

204
00:26:17,951 --> 00:26:20,287
Platform 8.

205
00:26:20,370 --> 00:26:22,581
I have a three-inch version of you 
on my shelf.

206
00:26:22,706 --> 00:26:25,500
Combatants 3 and 11.

207
00:26:25,667 --> 00:26:27,377
Disk wars.

208
00:26:27,003 --> 00:26:29,255
You definitely didn't do that.

209
00:27:00,911 --> 00:27:01,996
Damn it!

210
00:27:10,921 --> 00:27:12,381
So that's how it is.

211
00:27:29,148 --> 00:27:32,485
Combatant 11, de-resolution.

212
00:27:33,402 --> 00:27:36,322
I won. Now let me out!

213
00:27:36,447 --> 00:27:40,284
Combatant 3, round one, victory.

214
00:27:41,076 --> 00:27:43,120
No unusual activity on the Grid.

215
00:27:43,245 --> 00:27:44,705
Security sweeps and patrols

216
00:27:44,872 --> 00:27:47,374
have been intensified. 
Rectifier on schedule.

217
00:27:47,458 --> 00:27:51,337
Your initiative should be 
fully operational within 12 cycles.

218
00:27:53,005 --> 00:27:55,508
Perhaps if you were to include me

219
00:27:55,633 --> 00:28:00,221
in this initiative, 
I could be of even greater service.

220
00:28:00,304 --> 00:28:01,430
Combatants 3 and 7, disk wars.

221
00:28:01,430 --> 00:28:04,558
Combatants 3 and 7, disk wars.

222
00:28:07,311 --> 00:28:08,938
Initiate.

223
00:28:12,108 --> 00:28:15,486
Yeah. I'm out.

224
00:28:22,326 --> 00:28:24,453
Combatant 3, victory.

225
00:28:29,500 --> 00:28:31,669
Combatant 3, violation.

226
00:28:32,837 --> 00:28:36,465
Combatant 6, de-resolution.

227
00:28:36,549 --> 00:28:38,592
What is that program?

228
00:28:39,677 --> 00:28:41,137
Combatant 3,

229
00:28:41,262 --> 00:28:43,222
violation.

230
00:28:48,519 --> 00:28:50,604
Initiate final round.

231
00:28:55,109 --> 00:28:58,154
Combatant 3 versus Rinzler.

232
00:28:58,237 --> 00:29:00,781
Rinzler!

233
00:29:00,865 --> 00:29:02,408
Rinzler!

234
00:29:05,452 --> 00:29:07,163
You gotta be kidding me.

235
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:08,789
Rinzler!

236
00:29:10,374 --> 00:29:12,126
Rinzler!

237
00:29:12,877 --> 00:29:14,211
Rinzler!

238
00:29:15,588 --> 00:29:16,672
Rinzler!

239
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:19,049
Rinzler!

240
00:29:27,057 --> 00:29:29,059
Come on. Is that even legal?

241
00:30:02,593 --> 00:30:05,471
Why do I feel like I just got dumped on?

242
00:30:11,477 --> 00:30:14,146
Come on. Huh? Come on.

243
00:30:56,730 --> 00:30:58,357
De-rez!

244
00:30:59,775 --> 00:31:01,360
De-rez!

245
00:31:02,319 --> 00:31:03,612
De-rez!

246
00:31:07,992 --> 00:31:10,077
User.

247
00:31:21,171 --> 00:31:23,882
Identify yourself, program.

248
00:31:25,175 --> 00:31:27,428
I'm not a program.

249
00:31:32,975 --> 00:31:34,518
Identify.

250
00:31:36,186 --> 00:31:38,605
My name is Sam Flynn.

251
00:31:42,943 --> 00:31:45,112
Bring him to me.

252
00:31:47,698 --> 00:31:48,741
Let me go.

253
00:31:52,703 --> 00:31:54,038
Freaks.

254
00:31:56,248 --> 00:31:57,249
Where am I?

255
00:32:00,169 --> 00:32:02,671
Am I on the Grid?

256
00:32:04,048 --> 00:32:05,632
Who are you?

257
00:32:11,221 --> 00:32:12,306
Dad.

258
00:32:12,890 --> 00:32:14,641
Sam.

259
00:32:14,725 --> 00:32:17,853
Look at you, man. 
Look at the size of you.

260
00:32:19,897 --> 00:32:23,525
- How did you get in here? 
- I got your message.

261
00:32:23,650 --> 00:32:26,570
Oh. So it's just you?

262
00:32:27,571 --> 00:32:28,530
Yeah.

263
00:32:28,655 --> 00:32:32,493
Just you. Oh.

264
00:32:32,576 --> 00:32:35,329
Isn't this something?

265
00:32:35,412 --> 00:32:36,663
You look the same.

266
00:32:36,747 --> 00:32:39,875
A lot's happened, Sam. 
More than you can imagine. Disk.

267
00:32:45,214 --> 00:32:46,840
Let's have a look.

268
00:33:02,773 --> 00:33:04,274
Got it.

269
00:33:04,775 --> 00:33:06,902
Hmm. I expected more.

270
00:33:10,614 --> 00:33:13,325
So, you were trapped in here.

271
00:33:13,450 --> 00:33:14,910
That's right.

272
00:33:18,122 --> 00:33:21,166
- And you're in charge. 
- Right again. You're two for two.

273
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:24,545
So can we just go home now?

274
00:33:26,004 --> 00:33:27,840
Not in the cards.

275
00:33:28,966 --> 00:33:30,300
Not for you.

276
00:33:34,471 --> 00:33:36,765
That's a hell of a way to treat your son.

277
00:33:38,725 --> 00:33:40,602
Oh, that.

278
00:33:45,274 --> 00:33:47,734
I'm not your father, Sam.

279
00:33:49,653 --> 00:33:52,906
But I'm very, very happy to see you.

280
00:33:56,201 --> 00:33:58,120
Clu.

281
00:34:00,873 --> 00:34:02,082
Where is he?

282
00:34:02,207 --> 00:34:04,293
What did you do to him?

283
00:34:04,418 --> 00:34:08,964
Same thing I'm going to do to you, user.

284
00:34:31,069 --> 00:34:33,739
Greetings, programs.

285
00:34:36,450 --> 00:34:40,037
Oh, what an occasion 
we have here before us.

286
00:34:40,662 --> 00:34:44,500
Because your rumors are true.

287
00:34:44,625 --> 00:34:49,421
We do indeed have in our midst

288
00:34:49,546 --> 00:34:51,632
a user!

289
00:34:53,842 --> 00:34:56,511
A user.

290
00:34:58,889 --> 00:35:01,141
So, what to do?

291
00:35:01,934 --> 00:35:06,522
What does this user deserve?

292
00:35:06,605 --> 00:35:08,941
Might I suggest perhaps 
the challenge of the Grid?

293
00:35:16,114 --> 00:35:21,078
And who best to battle 
this singular opponent?

294
00:35:22,412 --> 00:35:26,542
Perhaps one who has some 
experience in these matters.

295
00:35:29,878 --> 00:35:31,672
Oh, yes, indeed, programs.

296
00:35:32,589 --> 00:35:35,050
Your liberator!

297
00:35:35,175 --> 00:35:36,760
Your luminary!

298
00:35:38,262 --> 00:35:40,013
Your leader and maker!

299
00:35:41,765 --> 00:35:45,310
The one who vanquished 
the tyranny of the user

300
00:35:46,061 --> 00:35:48,730
those many cycles before!

301
00:35:49,773 --> 00:35:52,317
I've been waiting 
a long time for this.

302
00:35:52,442 --> 00:35:55,988
Clu!

303
00:35:56,113 --> 00:35:59,241
You wanna play? I'll play.

304
00:36:16,758 --> 00:36:18,635
What's this?

305
00:36:18,719 --> 00:36:20,512
What do I do with this?

306
00:36:20,637 --> 00:36:22,681
I'll give you a hint.

307
00:36:23,557 --> 00:36:24,975
Not that.

308
00:36:34,860 --> 00:36:36,320
Grid is live.

309
00:36:36,445 --> 00:36:39,906
Initiate light cycle battle.

310
00:36:54,796 --> 00:36:56,131
You got no chance, user.

311
00:36:56,256 --> 00:36:59,426
Their bikes are faster than ours. 
Use the levels.

312
00:37:04,765 --> 00:37:06,850
Now this I can do.

313
00:37:39,257 --> 00:37:40,676
Here we go.

314
00:38:46,700 --> 00:38:48,118
Come on. Come on!

315
00:39:04,468 --> 00:39:07,429
Hey! We gotta work together.

316
00:39:07,554 --> 00:39:09,514
It's the only way.

317
00:39:17,606 --> 00:39:20,150
That's it. You got me.

318
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:29,451
Boo!

319
00:39:32,537 --> 00:39:33,830
- Whoo-hoo! 
- Yeah!

320
00:39:33,914 --> 00:39:36,041
Now that's what I'm talking about.

321
00:39:36,374 --> 00:39:38,835
Another customer. Let's go!

322
00:39:56,436 --> 00:39:57,854
Hang on, buddy, I'm coming.

323
00:40:06,988 --> 00:40:08,114
Come on.

324
00:40:40,522 --> 00:40:42,440
Illegal combatant on the Grid.

325
00:40:42,524 --> 00:40:43,942
Get in.

326
00:40:44,025 --> 00:40:45,569
Illegal combatant on the Grid.

327
00:40:45,694 --> 00:40:46,820
Get in!

328
00:40:53,034 --> 00:40:56,246
System failure. Release Rinzler.

329
00:40:56,371 --> 00:40:58,331
Game on, old friend.

330
00:41:07,590 --> 00:41:10,844
- Who are you? 
- Hang on.

331
00:41:38,830 --> 00:41:40,373
Pull up, man, you can't make that!

332
00:41:49,966 --> 00:41:52,344
Made it.

333
00:42:01,436 --> 00:42:02,604
I'm Quorra.

334
00:42:08,109 --> 00:42:09,319
They're turning around.

335
00:42:09,444 --> 00:42:10,779
Not by choice.

336
00:42:10,904 --> 00:42:14,449
Their vehicles can't go off Grid. 
They'll malfunction on this terrain.

337
00:42:14,574 --> 00:42:17,911
- What about us? 
- Obviously not.

338
00:42:32,384 --> 00:42:33,968
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

339
00:43:33,570 --> 00:43:35,613
Wait here.

340
00:43:38,992 --> 00:43:40,410
Quorra.

341
00:43:41,494 --> 00:43:43,455
I dreamed of Tron.

342
00:43:44,581 --> 00:43:46,583
First time in years.

343
00:43:47,083 --> 00:43:48,668
It's a sign.

344
00:43:50,003 --> 00:43:53,339
A sign, my dear apprentice, 
of a weary soul.

345
00:43:54,507 --> 00:43:57,719
- I'm afraid something's happened. 
- Something has happened.

346
00:43:59,053 --> 00:44:00,638
We have a guest.

347
00:44:02,098 --> 00:44:04,601
There are no guests, kiddo.

348
00:44:28,208 --> 00:44:30,251
Sam...

349
00:44:31,336 --> 00:44:33,671
Long time.

350
00:44:35,173 --> 00:44:38,009
You have no idea.

351
00:44:43,765 --> 00:44:46,351
You're... You're here.

352
00:44:50,438 --> 00:44:51,898
You're here.

353
00:44:52,774 --> 00:44:55,193
I'm here.

354
00:45:02,784 --> 00:45:04,327
You're big.

355
00:45:05,745 --> 00:45:07,539
You're...

356
00:45:08,289 --> 00:45:09,624
Old.

357
00:45:13,336 --> 00:45:15,588
How did you get here?

358
00:45:15,713 --> 00:45:18,174
Alan came over.

359
00:45:18,925 --> 00:45:20,635
Bradley.

360
00:45:20,760 --> 00:45:23,555
Yeah. He got your page.

361
00:45:23,638 --> 00:45:26,891
I found your office under the arcade.

362
00:45:28,309 --> 00:45:29,769
Page...

363
00:45:30,937 --> 00:45:32,188
Oh, the page.

364
00:45:33,523 --> 00:45:35,108
Of course.

365
00:45:39,195 --> 00:45:41,281
Clu had him on the light cycle grid.

366
00:45:41,406 --> 00:45:43,533
I intervened.

367
00:45:44,200 --> 00:45:45,243
Oh.

368
00:45:47,370 --> 00:45:48,371
Dinner soon.

369
00:45:49,330 --> 00:45:51,749
We'll talk then.

370
00:46:05,722 --> 00:46:08,933
He never thought he'd see you again.

371
00:46:11,144 --> 00:46:12,812
Yeah.

372
00:46:19,986 --> 00:46:24,324
Vintage. Flynn built it 
many cycles ago for the games.

373
00:46:25,408 --> 00:46:28,286
It doesn't get out 
as much as it used to,

374
00:46:28,369 --> 00:46:31,331
but it's still the fastest thing on the Grid.

375
00:46:53,561 --> 00:46:55,939
Your move, Flynn, come on.

376
00:46:56,856 --> 00:46:59,359
Come on!

377
00:47:17,669 --> 00:47:21,965
- How old are you now, Sam? 
- You should be 27.

378
00:47:23,050 --> 00:47:25,010
Yes, 27.

379
00:47:25,135 --> 00:47:28,513
- Do you attend a college? 
- Caltech.

380
00:47:29,890 --> 00:47:33,643
Caltech. My alma mater.

381
00:47:33,769 --> 00:47:35,062
Yeah.

382
00:47:35,145 --> 00:47:36,772
Till I dropped out.

383
00:47:46,239 --> 00:47:47,407
Work?

384
00:47:48,075 --> 00:47:50,869
- Job? ENCOM? Are you... 
- No.

385
00:47:53,163 --> 00:47:55,540
I check in once a year.

386
00:47:56,958 --> 00:47:59,086
- Wife, girlfriend? 
- Dog.

387
00:47:59,586 --> 00:48:01,922
Marvin.

388
00:48:02,005 --> 00:48:04,132
- A rescue. 
- Well, dogs...

389
00:48:04,216 --> 00:48:05,967
Dogs are cool.

390
00:48:15,018 --> 00:48:18,939
I'm sure you must have 
a few questions of your own, Sam.

391
00:48:21,274 --> 00:48:23,318
Actually, just one.

392
00:48:26,696 --> 00:48:28,657
Why I never came home.

393
00:48:32,536 --> 00:48:35,288
Those nights when I went to the office,

394
00:48:35,372 --> 00:48:38,667
I'm sure you've figured it out by now, 
I was coming here.

395
00:48:39,835 --> 00:48:42,629
Human form into digital space.

396
00:48:42,712 --> 00:48:44,756
Heavy stuff.

397
00:48:46,758 --> 00:48:48,969
But I also had you.

398
00:48:49,052 --> 00:48:52,514
I had ENCOM. 
I couldn't be in here all the time.

399
00:48:52,597 --> 00:48:55,308
I needed partners to help out.

400
00:48:55,392 --> 00:48:57,060
Tron and Clu?

401
00:48:57,894 --> 00:48:59,020
That's right.

402
00:49:01,731 --> 00:49:05,193
Tron was created by Alan 
for the old system.

403
00:49:05,277 --> 00:49:07,404
I brought him here to protect this one.

404
00:49:07,529 --> 00:49:09,739
Clu was my creation.

405
00:49:09,865 --> 00:49:13,660
A program designed 
to create a perfect world.

406
00:49:13,743 --> 00:49:17,539
We were jamming, man, 
building utopia.

407
00:49:17,664 --> 00:49:20,167
Hours in here 
were just minutes back home.

408
00:49:20,250 --> 00:49:23,044
Just when I thought 
it couldn't get any more profound,

409
00:49:23,128 --> 00:49:25,297
something unexpected happened.

410
00:49:25,964 --> 00:49:27,215
The miracle.

411
00:49:27,966 --> 00:49:29,885
The miracle.

412
00:49:29,968 --> 00:49:31,595
You remember.

413
00:49:32,929 --> 00:49:36,099
ISOs. Isomorphic algorithms.

414
00:49:36,933 --> 00:49:40,645
- A whole new life form. 
- And you created them?

415
00:49:45,275 --> 00:49:46,735
No. No.

416
00:49:46,818 --> 00:49:50,405
They manifested, like a flame.

417
00:49:50,489 --> 00:49:53,408
They weren't really from anywhere.

418
00:49:53,492 --> 00:49:56,369
The conditions were right 
and they came into being.

419
00:49:57,454 --> 00:50:01,249
For centuries we've dreamed 
of gods, spirits, aliens,

420
00:50:01,416 --> 00:50:03,418
an intelligence beyond our own.

421
00:50:03,501 --> 00:50:04,794
You seeing this?

422
00:50:04,920 --> 00:50:09,549
I found them in here. 
Like flowers in a wasteland.

423
00:50:12,469 --> 00:50:15,013
Profoundly naive.

424
00:50:16,765 --> 00:50:19,476
Unimaginably wise.

425
00:50:21,186 --> 00:50:23,396
They were spectacular.

426
00:50:23,480 --> 00:50:26,274
Everything I'd hoped to find 
in the system,

427
00:50:26,399 --> 00:50:28,902
control, order, perfection,

428
00:50:28,985 --> 00:50:30,362
none of it meant a thing.

429
00:50:30,487 --> 00:50:31,738
I'd been living in a hall of mirrors.

430
00:50:32,781 --> 00:50:35,450
The ISOs shattered it.

431
00:50:35,534 --> 00:50:39,120
The possibilities of their root code, 
their digital DNA.

432
00:50:39,204 --> 00:50:41,623
Disease? History.

433
00:50:42,415 --> 00:50:44,042
Science, philosophy,

434
00:50:44,167 --> 00:50:48,338
every idea man has ever had 
about the universe up for grabs.

435
00:50:48,463 --> 00:50:51,258
Bio-digital jazz, man.

436
00:50:52,050 --> 00:50:55,595
The IS Os, they were going 
to be my gift to the world.

437
00:50:55,679 --> 00:50:58,014
So what happened?

438
00:50:58,139 --> 00:51:01,559
Clu. Clu happened.

439
00:51:04,771 --> 00:51:07,524
Your transport to the portal 
is waiting for you.

440
00:51:07,649 --> 00:51:09,776
I don't like it when you cut it this close.

441
00:51:09,859 --> 00:51:13,905
Will you stop worrying, Tron? 
Everything's just fine.

442
00:51:14,030 --> 00:51:16,157
- Everything's under control. 
- Flynn!

443
00:51:23,766 --> 00:51:26,728
Tron, he fought for me.

444
00:51:28,187 --> 00:51:30,440
I never saw him again.

445
00:51:31,274 --> 00:51:32,942
So why didn't you fight?

446
00:51:33,443 --> 00:51:35,445
- Hmm. 
- He did.

447
00:51:35,570 --> 00:51:37,322
Clu fed on my resistance.

448
00:51:37,405 --> 00:51:40,116
The more I fought, 
the more powerful he became.

449
00:51:40,700 --> 00:51:42,910
It was impressive, really.

450
00:51:43,536 --> 00:51:48,416
And my miracle... 
Clu saw the IS Os as an imperfection.

451
00:51:49,042 --> 00:51:50,960
So he destroyed them.

452
00:51:54,213 --> 00:51:55,882
The Purge.

453
00:51:56,424 --> 00:52:00,386
- He killed them all? 
- It was genocide.

454
00:52:01,012 --> 00:52:04,599
I tried to get back 
but I couldn't get to the portal.

455
00:52:05,183 --> 00:52:09,604
It uses massive power 
and it can't stay open forever.

456
00:52:10,438 --> 00:52:12,732
And like a safe, it...

457
00:52:12,815 --> 00:52:15,568
It can only be opened from the outside.

458
00:52:17,570 --> 00:52:20,365
It closed on me, Sam.

459
00:52:20,948 --> 00:52:23,326
That's why I never came home.

460
00:52:30,333 --> 00:52:32,502
So the portal, it activated

461
00:52:32,627 --> 00:52:35,380
when I came in. So it's open now.

462
00:52:35,463 --> 00:52:36,464
Not for long.

463
00:52:36,589 --> 00:52:39,175
Only one millicycle, about eight hours.

464
00:52:39,300 --> 00:52:42,637
So we go now. Go home. 
We make a run for it.

465
00:52:42,762 --> 00:52:44,889
- We get you out of here. 
- Don't rush.

466
00:52:44,972 --> 00:52:47,141
What do you mean? 
The portal's gonna close.

467
00:52:49,352 --> 00:52:50,937
What? What is it?

468
00:52:51,062 --> 00:52:55,108
The moment Flynn is on the Grid, Clu 
will stop at nothing to obtain his disk.

469
00:52:55,233 --> 00:52:57,276
My disk is everything, Sam.

470
00:52:57,402 --> 00:53:00,822
It's the master key. The golden ticket. 
The way out.

471
00:53:01,989 --> 00:53:05,451
- And not just for me. 
- What do you mean?

472
00:53:05,576 --> 00:53:08,287
Our worlds are more connected 
than anyone knows.

473
00:53:08,371 --> 00:53:10,581
Clu figures if I can be in...

474
00:53:10,665 --> 00:53:12,333
He can be out?

475
00:53:12,458 --> 00:53:16,003
- With my disk, it's possible. 
- And then what?

476
00:53:16,671 --> 00:53:18,381
Game over.

477
00:53:19,215 --> 00:53:22,009
The guy doesn't dig imperfection.

478
00:53:23,553 --> 00:53:26,013
What's more imperfect than our world?

479
00:53:27,598 --> 00:53:30,893
I can't let that happen. I won't.

480
00:53:31,352 --> 00:53:34,522
So what do we do? Nothing?

481
00:53:34,647 --> 00:53:37,567
It's amazing how productive 
doing nothing can be.

482
00:53:37,692 --> 00:53:41,279
Clu's planning something. 
We've known that for a while.

483
00:53:41,696 --> 00:53:43,030
Programs have been disappearing.

484
00:53:43,156 --> 00:53:45,783
There's unrest out there, 
even revolution.

485
00:53:45,867 --> 00:53:50,079
If we sit tight, Clu might 
be brought down from the inside.

486
00:53:50,204 --> 00:53:53,499
If the portal is closing, we can't 
sit around. We have to move now.

487
00:53:53,583 --> 00:53:58,379
Tell me, what brought you here, 
to the Grid?

488
00:53:58,921 --> 00:54:00,798
Alan got your page.

489
00:54:00,882 --> 00:54:03,634
I didn't send any page.

490
00:54:04,135 --> 00:54:05,344
It was Clu.

491
00:54:05,470 --> 00:54:08,347
Clu sent that page. 
That's why you're here.

492
00:54:08,431 --> 00:54:11,392
This is all his design. 
He wanted a new piece

493
00:54:11,517 --> 00:54:13,936
on the board to change the game!

494
00:54:14,061 --> 00:54:16,105
With you, he got more 
than he ever dreamed.

495
00:54:16,230 --> 00:54:21,360
This is precisely what he wants. 
Us together heading for the portal.

496
00:54:21,444 --> 00:54:25,573
It's his game now. 
The only way to win is not to play.

497
00:54:27,617 --> 00:54:29,535
Well, that's a hell of a way to live.

498
00:54:29,619 --> 00:54:31,204
But it is a way.

499
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:37,835
We can go home.

500
00:54:39,754 --> 00:54:41,672
Don't you want that?

501
00:54:42,340 --> 00:54:47,845
Sometimes life has a way of moving you 
past things like wants and hopes.

502
00:54:48,596 --> 00:54:53,267
That's great, Dad. 
Keep telling yourself that.

503
00:54:58,940 --> 00:55:00,107
Good night, Sam.

504
00:55:23,381 --> 00:55:25,675
How can he be so afraid 
of his own creation?

505
00:55:25,800 --> 00:55:28,928
I mean, he built Clu. 
Why doesn't he just end him?

506
00:55:30,263 --> 00:55:32,306
He could, 
but it would require reintegration.

507
00:55:32,431 --> 00:55:33,891
Yeah, all right.

508
00:55:33,975 --> 00:55:37,645
Flynn would never survive the event. 
It would mean the end of them both.

509
00:55:38,104 --> 00:55:41,399
If he refuses to save himself, 
then I will.

510
00:55:45,611 --> 00:55:47,280
How?

511
00:55:47,363 --> 00:55:49,824
I'm going through the portal.

512
00:55:49,949 --> 00:55:51,659
Clu wants Flynn's disk, not mine.

513
00:55:51,784 --> 00:55:56,372
I'm going to find Alan and we'll figure 
this thing out from the other side.

514
00:55:56,497 --> 00:55:59,917
This may be Clu's game here, but 
in my world, he's gone in one keystroke.

515
00:56:00,001 --> 00:56:03,296
But I can't do anything 
unless I get to the portal.

516
00:56:04,672 --> 00:56:05,756
And my guts tell me

517
00:56:05,840 --> 00:56:09,886
that you don't want to be stuck 
in this place for eternity either.

518
00:56:11,846 --> 00:56:13,723
There's someone I once knew,

519
00:56:13,848 --> 00:56:16,934
a program named Zuse 
who fought alongside the ISOs.

520
00:56:17,059 --> 00:56:20,313
They say he can get anyone anywhere.

521
00:56:22,064 --> 00:56:24,025
How do I find him?

522
00:56:26,986 --> 00:56:28,821
This is his sector.

523
00:56:32,158 --> 00:56:35,161
Make it there alive, and he'll find you.

524
00:57:15,910 --> 00:57:17,495
Sam?

525
00:57:21,123 --> 00:57:22,375
Sam?

526
00:57:54,532 --> 00:57:58,452
All programs are required 
to present identity disks

527
00:57:58,577 --> 00:57:59,996
at city checkpoints.

528
00:58:04,333 --> 00:58:06,877
Hey, man. It's your lucky day.

529
00:58:13,843 --> 00:58:16,929
- Any program without their disk... 
- Stop him!

530
00:58:17,012 --> 00:58:19,390
...will be taken into custody.

531
00:58:21,100 --> 00:58:26,021
Any program in violation of their 
function is subject to termination.

532
00:58:26,564 --> 00:58:30,025
Sam Flynn? 
You remember me?

533
00:58:30,359 --> 00:58:34,321
- Yeah. You gave me some advice. 
- And you followed it.

534
00:58:35,781 --> 00:58:38,409
It's unfortunate we met the way we did.

535
00:58:39,744 --> 00:58:41,078
You have a good night.

536
00:58:41,203 --> 00:58:43,664
You're looking for someone.

537
00:58:46,333 --> 00:58:48,294
What makes you say that?

538
00:58:49,211 --> 00:58:51,172
Intuition.

539
00:58:53,215 --> 00:58:57,428
Sir, the sentries downtown 
have recovered Flynn's light cycle.

540
00:58:58,763 --> 00:59:02,057
We've traced it to its point of origin.

541
00:59:27,041 --> 00:59:29,919
Prepare the light runner, 
Quorra.

542
00:59:30,628 --> 00:59:33,172
We're going downtown.

543
00:59:55,569 --> 00:59:57,279
Thank you for bringing my son to me.

544
00:59:57,404 --> 00:59:58,614
Flynn!

545
00:59:58,739 --> 01:00:01,659
You don't need to go. 
I've sent him to someone we can trust.

546
01:00:01,784 --> 01:00:03,869
Quorra, there is no choice.

547
01:00:04,787 --> 01:00:06,914
I won't lose him again.

548
01:00:08,958 --> 01:00:12,127
Chaos. Good news.

549
01:00:53,043 --> 01:00:56,714
His name is Castor. If you want to speak 
to Zuse, you need to go through him.

550
01:00:56,839 --> 01:00:59,466
Where's your sense of humor, 
my friend?

551
01:00:59,550 --> 01:01:02,845
Programs are disappearing. 
Soon none of us will be left.

552
01:01:02,970 --> 01:01:05,681
Zuse can unite the factions, 
foment revolution.

553
01:01:05,764 --> 01:01:09,226
- Of course Zuse can do these things. 
- Grant me an audience.

554
01:01:09,310 --> 01:01:12,521
Your enthusiasm is intoxicating, 
my dear Bartik,

555
01:01:12,605 --> 01:01:15,316
but Zuse's time is precious.

556
01:01:17,318 --> 01:01:19,403
I brought your boy Flynn.

557
01:01:19,528 --> 01:01:24,533
If you'll excuse me for a moment, 
I have to attend to something.

558
01:01:24,658 --> 01:01:27,870
But have a drink, 
courtesy of the End of Line Club!

559
01:01:28,621 --> 01:01:29,622
It is happening.

560
01:01:31,040 --> 01:01:33,459
I'm looking for Zuse.

561
01:01:33,542 --> 01:01:36,420
Indeed. Many are.

562
01:01:36,545 --> 01:01:38,464
Where can I find him?

563
01:01:38,547 --> 01:01:42,509
This, pretty miss, is a conversation 
best had behind closed doors.

564
01:02:12,682 --> 01:02:15,435
- You are Clu. 
- I am Clu.

565
01:02:15,560 --> 01:02:20,315
- You will create the perfect system. 
- I will create the perfect system.

566
01:02:23,860 --> 01:02:26,905
Together we're gonna 
change the world, man.

567
01:02:37,165 --> 01:02:38,708
Zuse has been around

568
01:02:38,833 --> 01:02:40,752
since the earliest days 
of the gaming grid.

569
01:02:41,211 --> 01:02:45,340
By necessity, 
he has to mind all the percentages.

570
01:02:45,423 --> 01:02:47,342
All the angles.

571
01:02:47,425 --> 01:02:49,260
So when do I meet him?

572
01:02:55,141 --> 01:02:59,020
After the Purge, 
I needed to reinvent myself.

573
01:02:59,104 --> 01:03:01,314
Self-preservation, you understand.

574
01:03:06,403 --> 01:03:10,991
Now, what can I do for you?

575
01:03:13,743 --> 01:03:15,745
I need to get to the portal.

576
01:03:15,870 --> 01:03:17,330
Well, it's closing quickly,

577
01:03:17,414 --> 01:03:20,041
as I'm sure you're aware.

578
01:03:20,166 --> 01:03:21,626
Tick-tock, tick-tock.

579
01:03:21,751 --> 01:03:24,003
And it's quite the journey.

580
01:03:24,087 --> 01:03:26,840
Beyond the far reaches of the Outlands.

581
01:03:26,965 --> 01:03:31,428
Your father didn't want any programs 
slipping out accidentally, did he?

582
01:03:42,647 --> 01:03:45,233
This is going to be quite the ride.

583
01:03:58,496 --> 01:03:59,748
Resist!

584
01:04:27,150 --> 01:04:28,526
Yeah!

585
01:05:08,233 --> 01:05:09,818
Go, go!

586
01:05:15,240 --> 01:05:17,325
Let's split, man.

587
01:05:37,595 --> 01:05:38,555
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

588
01:06:02,370 --> 01:06:03,621
Your disk.

589
01:06:04,664 --> 01:06:05,707
Dad, it's gone.

590
01:06:06,833 --> 01:06:08,001
It is.

591
01:06:10,962 --> 01:06:12,589
I'm sorry. I know I messed up.

592
01:06:14,799 --> 01:06:15,758
We can go back.

593
01:06:18,279 --> 01:06:20,490
You're messing with my Zen thing, man.

594
01:06:23,117 --> 01:06:24,202
She's stable.

595
01:06:30,750 --> 01:06:33,586
You ever jump a freight train?

596
01:06:34,796 --> 01:06:35,797
Huh?

597
01:06:35,880 --> 01:06:39,050
We do it your way. 
Full-on sprint to the portal.

598
01:06:39,175 --> 01:06:41,010
If we beat Clu there, we have a chance.

599
01:06:41,135 --> 01:06:42,428
Let's get her out of here.

600
01:06:59,130 --> 01:07:01,758
I've got to identify the damaged code.

601
01:07:01,883 --> 01:07:05,428
The sequencing 
is just enormously complex.

602
01:07:06,554 --> 01:07:11,226
- But didn't you write it? 
- Some of it. The rest of it is just

603
01:07:16,166 --> 01:07:18,251
Yeah.

604
01:07:20,045 --> 01:07:22,464
Check that out.

605
01:07:30,639 --> 01:07:32,724
She risked herself for me.

606
01:07:34,684 --> 01:07:36,978
Some things are worth the risk.

607
01:07:50,617 --> 01:07:52,536
Look at this.

608
01:07:55,413 --> 01:07:59,000
Now, that is impressive 
if I do say so myself. Huh?

609
01:08:00,460 --> 01:08:03,630
Come on, it's gonna take a while 
for her system to reboot.

610
01:08:03,713 --> 01:08:06,883
Now it's time for you to tell me a story.

611
01:08:09,344 --> 01:08:11,471
Mom and Dad are...

612
01:08:13,223 --> 01:08:15,433
- I assume that... 
- Yeah.

613
01:08:16,643 --> 01:08:17,644
Oh.

614
01:08:18,728 --> 01:08:21,064
Mac when I was 12

615
01:08:21,189 --> 01:08:24,067
and Gram five years later.

616
01:08:26,862 --> 01:08:30,699
You remember that night 
when you didn't come home?

617
01:08:30,824 --> 01:08:31,992
- Well... 
- You said...

618
01:08:32,117 --> 01:08:34,160
I said I'd show you the Grid.

619
01:08:36,246 --> 01:08:38,540
You should have seen this place 
back then.

620
01:08:39,541 --> 01:08:44,838
I couldn't wait to show it to you. 
Could not wait.

621
01:08:44,921 --> 01:08:47,424
Must have been something 
before Clu screwed it up.

622
01:08:47,549 --> 01:08:49,217
No, no, he...

623
01:08:51,052 --> 01:08:53,680
He's me. I screwed it up.

624
01:08:55,223 --> 01:08:57,309
Chasing after perfection.

625
01:08:59,394 --> 01:09:03,064
Chasing after 
what was right in front of me.

626
01:09:03,690 --> 01:09:05,567
Right in front of me.

627
01:09:07,485 --> 01:09:09,821
Look what you've accomplished.

628
01:09:10,238 --> 01:09:11,990
It's incredible.

629
01:09:12,073 --> 01:09:13,450
Sam,

630
01:09:17,787 --> 01:09:21,749
- Yeah, well, I'm fixing her up. 
- You busted my bike?

631
01:09:21,833 --> 01:09:27,505
Twenty years in the shed, no tarp. 
I mean, she needed a little love.

632
01:09:29,132 --> 01:09:30,675
How does she run?

633
01:09:32,427 --> 01:09:34,929
Well, man, I'd like to see that.

634
01:09:36,597 --> 01:09:38,099
You will.

635
01:09:41,519 --> 01:09:42,520
Here.

636
01:09:42,854 --> 01:09:45,314
She's rebooting. Give her this.

637
01:09:45,398 --> 01:09:49,193
The old man's gonna knock on the sky, 
listen to the sound.

638
01:10:11,692 --> 01:10:14,737
Hey. It's okay. We're safe for now.

639
01:10:14,862 --> 01:10:17,448
We're heading east towards the portal.

640
01:10:20,201 --> 01:10:22,078
Clu has the disk.

641
01:10:22,745 --> 01:10:25,581
Once I get out, I can shut him down.

642
01:10:27,750 --> 01:10:31,254
I should never have sent you to Zuse. 
It was a mistake.

643
01:10:31,379 --> 01:10:33,840
It's okay. I've made a few myself.

644
01:10:36,528 --> 01:10:38,613
And listening to the sound.

645
01:10:39,906 --> 01:10:41,241
Yeah.

646
01:10:41,908 --> 01:10:43,869
How did you find him?

647
01:10:51,501 --> 01:10:52,919
I know.

648
01:10:58,174 --> 01:11:00,468
It was during the Purge.

649
01:11:01,678 --> 01:11:03,596
Clu was relentless.

650
01:11:03,138 --> 01:11:05,057
So I ran.

651
01:11:06,141 --> 01:11:09,436
A sympathetic program 
smuggled me out of the city.

652
01:11:09,519 --> 01:11:12,022
But soon they had me surrounded.

653
01:11:15,401 --> 01:11:19,738
standing above me was the Creator.

654
01:11:22,408 --> 01:11:24,159
Your father.

655
01:11:25,786 --> 01:11:27,413
He saved me.

656
01:11:31,709 --> 01:11:35,170
I guess you could say I'm a rescue.

657
01:11:54,273 --> 01:11:56,066
Hell of a view.

658
01:11:56,233 --> 01:11:59,028
It used to let us know 
that Flynn was here.

659
01:11:59,111 --> 01:12:01,447
It became the symbol 
of something bigger,

660
01:12:01,613 --> 01:12:04,867
something better than this world.

661
01:12:05,659 --> 01:12:08,120
I've never been this close before.

662
01:12:09,288 --> 01:12:11,832
It's how I imagine a sunrise to be.

663
01:12:11,957 --> 01:12:14,251
Ah, trust me. There's no comparison.

664
01:12:17,713 --> 01:12:19,631
What's it like?

665
01:12:21,675 --> 01:12:24,136
- The sun? 
- Yeah.

666
01:12:25,012 --> 01:12:26,972
Man...

667
01:12:29,516 --> 01:12:30,684
Warm.

668
01:12:49,912 --> 01:12:52,623
Get below! Move!

669
01:12:54,500 --> 01:12:56,794
This isn't supposed to be here.

670
01:13:11,601 --> 01:13:12,977
What is this?

671
01:13:17,273 --> 01:13:18,774
He's building an army.

672
01:13:19,817 --> 01:13:21,110
Let's go.

673
01:13:21,235 --> 01:13:26,407
All high-level functions, 
report immediately to combat stations.

674
01:13:51,599 --> 01:13:53,851
- Goodbye. 
- Quorra!

675
01:13:54,351 --> 01:13:57,354
- What's she doing? 
- Removing herself from the equation.

676
01:14:15,497 --> 01:14:16,916
Tron.

677
01:14:18,709 --> 01:14:20,794
He's alive.

678
01:14:21,420 --> 01:14:23,881
Throne ship is approaching.

679
01:14:26,800 --> 01:14:30,471
- We can't just let her go. 
- No, Sam, there's another way.

680
01:14:31,180 --> 01:14:33,557
Throne ship is approaching.

681
01:14:44,818 --> 01:14:46,904
Well done, sir.

682
01:15:01,168 --> 01:15:03,629
I've never seen anything like it.

683
01:15:04,129 --> 01:15:07,758
Humbly, sir, I know 
you have greater designs

684
01:15:07,883 --> 01:15:10,427
than any of us understand.

685
01:15:11,637 --> 01:15:13,055
What does it do?

686
01:15:38,956 --> 01:15:40,833
She's gonna wind up like one of them.

687
01:15:41,375 --> 01:15:42,543
Keep moving, Sam.

688
01:15:53,220 --> 01:15:57,015
You are a very rare bird, 
aren't you, now?

689
01:16:05,274 --> 01:16:06,984
Where's your disk?

690
01:16:09,611 --> 01:16:11,405
Where is he?

691
01:16:13,323 --> 01:16:16,034
It must have been so lonely out there.

692
01:16:17,327 --> 01:16:19,913
How tragic to be the only one.

693
01:16:25,437 --> 01:16:26,855
He's taking all of this with him.

694
01:16:27,439 --> 01:16:29,274
He's figured out how to do it.

695
01:16:29,400 --> 01:16:31,277
And whatever we find there,

696
01:16:31,443 --> 01:16:33,570
there our system will grow!

697
01:16:33,654 --> 01:16:37,241
There our system will blossom!

698
01:16:38,492 --> 01:16:39,994
Do this.

699
01:16:40,119 --> 01:16:42,746
Prove yourselves. 
Prove yourselves to me!

700
01:16:42,830 --> 01:16:44,415
Be loyal to me!

701
01:16:44,957 --> 01:16:47,751
And I will never betray you!

702
01:17:00,347 --> 01:17:01,932
Dad, we have to get your disk.

703
01:17:02,141 --> 01:17:04,852
We gotta get to the portal. 
You shut them down outside.

704
01:17:04,977 --> 01:17:07,604
Even if I make it, you won't 
last in here, nor will Quorra.

705
01:17:07,730 --> 01:17:10,941
- We'll be all right. Come on. 
- I'm not going home without you.

706
01:17:12,109 --> 01:17:13,360
Sam...

707
01:17:13,944 --> 01:17:15,696
The same team.

708
01:17:16,655 --> 01:17:17,990
Remember?

709
01:17:20,159 --> 01:17:22,161
I was afraid you were gonna say that.

710
01:17:23,245 --> 01:17:25,331
Meet me on the flight deck in five 
and get us some wheels.

711
01:17:25,456 --> 01:17:27,624
Wheels? What's your plan?

712
01:17:28,500 --> 01:17:30,878
I'm a user. I'll improvise.

713
01:17:32,504 --> 01:17:34,423
Maximize efficiency.

714
01:17:35,841 --> 01:17:38,719
Rid the new system of its imperfection!

715
01:17:41,346 --> 01:17:44,850
My vision is clear, fellow programs.

716
01:17:45,851 --> 01:17:49,980
Out there is a new world!

717
01:17:50,731 --> 01:17:53,400
Out there is our victory!

718
01:17:54,860 --> 01:17:56,361
Out there

719
01:17:58,489 --> 01:18:00,949
is our destiny.

720
01:18:44,618 --> 01:18:47,287
Identify yourself, program.

721
01:19:15,667 --> 01:19:17,961
- Why are you here? 
- We gotta get to the flight deck.

722
01:19:18,086 --> 01:19:19,338
Clu will be here any minute.

723
01:19:19,463 --> 01:19:21,298
- We'll never make it. 
- Come on.

724
01:19:27,679 --> 01:19:29,014
Come on, kiddo.

725
01:19:32,684 --> 01:19:35,354
Radical, man.

726
01:19:43,195 --> 01:19:44,655
Hurry!

727
01:19:44,738 --> 01:19:46,406
Made it.

728
01:20:05,217 --> 01:20:08,220
Try and hold on to this. 
You're gonna need it.

729
01:20:13,267 --> 01:20:16,895
You got this, Quorra. It's all in the wrist.

730
01:20:31,827 --> 01:20:35,372
Light fighter 5. 
Unauthorized launch.

731
01:20:56,435 --> 01:20:58,478
Death to the user!

732
01:21:22,919 --> 01:21:24,129
Head towards the light, Quorra.

733
01:21:27,049 --> 01:21:28,842
Where did you learn that move?

734
01:21:28,967 --> 01:21:31,595
ENCOM Tower. Couple of nights ago.

735
01:21:34,097 --> 01:21:36,725
ENCOM Tower. Huh.

736
01:21:38,518 --> 01:21:39,728
Light jets.

737
01:21:40,312 --> 01:21:41,688
Here they come.

738
01:21:42,647 --> 01:21:45,025
- Sam, take the turret. 
- Huh?

739
01:21:53,283 --> 01:21:55,577
Man, I'm all over this.

740
01:21:58,538 --> 01:21:59,664
Yeah!

741
01:22:09,591 --> 01:22:12,844
Yeah! One down, five to go!

742
01:22:18,600 --> 01:22:19,601
Nice.

743
01:22:29,069 --> 01:22:30,237
We gotta split them up!

744
01:22:30,237 --> 01:22:30,987
We gotta split them up!

745
01:22:50,757 --> 01:22:52,134
Come on.

746
01:22:56,346 --> 01:22:58,390
Have a nice swim!

747
01:23:04,563 --> 01:23:06,565
We gotta get behind them!

748
01:23:07,232 --> 01:23:09,025
Whoo!

749
01:23:14,406 --> 01:23:17,576
- I don't think this is a good idea. 
- You're probably right.

750
01:23:23,415 --> 01:23:24,833
He's gaining on us!

751
01:23:55,655 --> 01:23:57,032
Yes!

752
01:24:08,585 --> 01:24:09,586
It's jammed.

753
01:24:15,217 --> 01:24:18,470
Tron. What have you become?

754
01:24:23,517 --> 01:24:24,810
Oh, come on.

755
01:24:28,021 --> 01:24:30,565
Flynn, go!

756
01:24:34,027 --> 01:24:36,238
Rinzler! Take the shot!

757
01:24:39,157 --> 01:24:40,826
Finish the game!

758
01:24:48,708 --> 01:24:50,669
Roll!

759
01:25:03,056 --> 01:25:05,767
I fight for the users.

760
01:25:15,735 --> 01:25:18,196
That's it. It's over.

761
01:25:19,197 --> 01:25:20,198
It's over!

762
01:25:22,367 --> 01:25:24,160
Whoo!

763
01:25:31,668 --> 01:25:34,796
Quorra, there's something 
I need you to do.

764
01:26:15,003 --> 01:26:16,922
Let's get you home, Dad.

765
01:26:20,967 --> 01:26:22,260
There it is.

766
01:26:22,927 --> 01:26:27,140
- Take her down. 
- Hang on. This could be rough.

767
01:27:12,411 --> 01:27:14,497
I had a feeling you'd be here!

768
01:27:14,664 --> 01:27:18,459
The cycles 
haven't been kind, have they?

769
01:27:19,377 --> 01:27:21,629
Oh, you don't look so bad.

770
01:27:22,963 --> 01:27:26,509
I did everything. 
Everything you ever asked.

771
01:27:27,134 --> 01:27:28,844
I know you did.

772
01:27:28,969 --> 01:27:32,264
- I executed the plan! 
- As you saw it.

773
01:27:39,456 --> 01:27:41,708
Remember what you came for.

774
01:27:55,722 --> 01:27:56,723
Dad!

775
01:27:56,848 --> 01:27:58,308
You knew I'd beat you.

776
01:27:58,475 --> 01:28:01,520
And still you did all this? For him.

777
01:28:07,692 --> 01:28:08,944
No.

778
01:28:14,533 --> 01:28:15,784
No!

779
01:28:15,909 --> 01:28:17,244
Why?

780
01:28:18,954 --> 01:28:20,288
He's my son.

781
01:28:26,670 --> 01:28:27,671
Go!

782
01:28:33,552 --> 01:28:34,636
Dad!

783
01:28:41,184 --> 01:28:43,311
Sam! It's time!

784
01:28:43,603 --> 01:28:44,729
No!

785
01:28:45,146 --> 01:28:47,857
Sam, it's what he wants.

786
01:28:49,943 --> 01:28:51,861
I'm not leaving you!

787
01:28:52,279 --> 01:28:53,738
Take her!

788
01:29:05,208 --> 01:29:06,793
Yes!

789
01:29:34,487 --> 01:29:36,156
Goodbye, kiddo.

790
01:30:07,479 --> 01:30:09,356
No!

791
01:31:20,301 --> 01:31:22,095
Al?

792
01:31:26,516 --> 01:31:28,309
You paged me?

793
01:31:28,852 --> 01:31:30,478
Yeah.

794
01:31:31,312 --> 01:31:33,565
I need you at ENCOM at 8:00 a.m.

795
01:31:35,525 --> 01:31:37,027
What about the board?

796
01:31:38,695 --> 01:31:40,613
You're chairman now.

797
01:31:42,949 --> 01:31:45,368
I'm taking the company back, Alan.

798
01:31:49,497 --> 01:31:50,665
Oh, and...

799
01:31:52,000 --> 01:31:53,626
You were right.

800
01:31:55,336 --> 01:31:56,713
About what?

801
01:31:58,381 --> 01:31:59,966
About everything.

802
01:32:47,514 --> 01:32:49,682
Software giant ENCOM International

803
01:32:49,766 --> 01:32:51,059
has reinstated 
Alan Bradley as chairman.

804
01:32:51,142 --> 01:32:52,644
The justice department 
announced today

805
01:32:52,727 --> 01:32:54,521
that it'll begin 
a full-on investigation

806
01:32:54,604 --> 01:32:57,398
into the underground movement 
known as "Flynn Lives"

807
01:32:57,482 --> 01:33:00,360
Lead by a mysterious 
online figure known as ZackAttack

808
01:33:00,443 --> 01:33:02,737
this renegade group 
has been held responsible

809
01:33:02,821 --> 01:33:05,240
for acts of subversion 
against ENCOM

810
01:33:05,448 --> 01:33:07,408
Flynn lives! Flynn lives!

811
01:33:07,742 --> 01:33:10,703
Greetings. My name is ZackAttack.

812
01:33:11,079 --> 01:33:13,957
Previously I have been communicating 
to you through message in code.

813
01:33:14,582 --> 01:33:17,001
But as of this morning 
the landscape has become

814
01:33:17,085 --> 01:33:19,671
too difficult and dangerous to operate in.

815
01:33:20,964 --> 01:33:22,257
I want to thank the millions of you

816
01:33:22,340 --> 01:33:25,135
who have helped to keep 
Kevin Flynn's spirit alive,

817
01:33:25,885 --> 01:33:29,973
And especially those of you 
who've been with us from the beginning.

818
01:34:08,720 --> 01:34:11,723
The "Flynn Lives" movement 
was born out of loss.

819
01:34:12,265 --> 01:34:15,184
But Kevin's genius inspired us all.

820
01:34:15,268 --> 01:34:18,605
He saw worlds beyond 
what we believed to be possible.

821
01:34:19,355 --> 01:34:22,984
When he disappeared 
that future was taken from all of us.

822
01:34:24,235 --> 01:34:26,487
Alan Bradley tried to continue 
Flynn's legacy.

823
01:34:27,280 --> 01:34:31,326
But when ENCOM started losing 
the software game to Dillinger Systems

824
01:34:32,160 --> 01:34:34,704
the shareholders demanded a change.

825
01:34:57,143 --> 01:34:58,853
ENCOM was founded 
around a chess game.

826
01:34:59,354 --> 01:35:02,148
Your plan represents 
everything Flynn was against.

827
01:35:02,273 --> 01:35:04,275
That spirit totally got away from the top brass.

828
01:35:04,817 --> 01:35:06,903
So we're all writing Flynn off.

829
01:35:07,612 --> 01:35:09,572
You'll have my resignation 
by the end of the day.

830
01:35:09,656 --> 01:35:11,574
How many employees 
are you letting go?

831
01:35:13,159 --> 01:35:15,536
With Flynn gone we were no longer 
in the video game business.

832
01:35:15,870 --> 01:35:17,330
It was all corporate.

833
01:35:17,413 --> 01:35:20,083
I knew it was over 
when they brought the cubicles back.

834
01:35:21,542 --> 01:35:24,504
I guess getting fired is the 
best thing that ever happened to me.

835
01:35:24,587 --> 01:35:27,382
But you were one of the first 
of ENCOM's employees ...

836
01:35:31,970 --> 01:35:33,972
Sure. I have this nickname.

837
01:35:34,055 --> 01:35:35,139
What do you want to start from? 
Just that?

838
01:35:35,223 --> 01:35:36,265
- That question?

839
01:35:37,558 --> 01:35:40,019
Anyway, we were talking about what? 
Oh, my TRON nickname.

840
01:35:40,103 --> 01:35:41,312
Right.

841
01:35:42,397 --> 01:35:47,193
I created a self monitoring 
computer security system back in '82.

842
01:35:47,277 --> 01:35:48,653
I called it TRON.

843
01:35:48,778 --> 01:35:49,946
Well the weird thing is ...

844
01:35:50,530 --> 01:35:52,115
Flynn took to calling me TRON.

845
01:35:52,365 --> 01:35:55,910
All the programmers ran with it 
and the nickname stayed with me for years.

846
01:35:57,537 --> 01:35:58,746
Speaking of which,

847
01:35:58,830 --> 01:36:01,541
it's been 7 years since 
you've last seen Kevin Flynn.

848
01:36:02,166 --> 01:36:05,795
Do you think there's anyone out there 
who still thinks he's alive?

849
01:36:17,307 --> 01:36:18,391
Mom, it's doing it again.

850
01:36:19,642 --> 01:36:23,855
You created the "Flynn Lives" virus 
that attacked 40 million PCs last year.

851
01:36:24,564 --> 01:36:27,400
I like to think of it as more of 
an easter egg than a virus.

852
01:36:28,026 --> 01:36:29,694
Was the group "Flynn Lives" involved?

853
01:36:29,777 --> 01:36:31,279
No. I acted alone.

854
01:36:31,988 --> 01:36:33,156
It was so cool.

855
01:36:37,160 --> 01:36:38,328
Are you ZackAttack?

856
01:36:40,830 --> 01:36:42,081
No.

857
01:36:42,415 --> 01:36:44,917
And if I was there's no way 
you would have ever found me.

858
01:36:45,001 --> 01:36:46,085
"Isolated Thinker"?

859
01:36:46,169 --> 01:36:48,755
Well, "Isolated Thinker" helped me 
pay my legal fees and kept me out of jail.

860
01:36:49,339 --> 01:36:51,841
But you did hack into the ENCOM mainframe

861
01:36:51,924 --> 01:36:53,259
on behalf of the group, correct?

862
01:36:53,343 --> 01:36:54,761
You can't talk about that.

863
01:36:56,721 --> 01:37:00,308
How do you feel about the 
"Flynn Lives" movement now, today?

864
01:37:00,391 --> 01:37:02,935
What movement? It's totally dead.

865
01:37:06,647 --> 01:37:10,777
Publicly ENCOM and I have acknowledged 
the fact that he is gone.

866
01:37:11,611 --> 01:37:15,490
His disappearance was a massive blow, 
personally and professionally.

867
01:37:15,490 --> 01:37:17,992
This was a man with an entire world

868
01:37:18,159 --> 01:37:19,994
waiting to see what he was going to do next.

869
01:37:20,078 --> 01:37:23,915
So, yeah, I think something's a little weird 
that he just totally vanishes.

870
01:37:23,998 --> 01:37:25,166
Well, I don't think he's dead.

871
01:37:25,708 --> 01:37:29,420
Is there anyone in the movement 
who has seen Kevin Flynn alive and well?

872
01:37:29,504 --> 01:37:32,673
- Where do you think he is? 
- I don't know. They know!

873
01:37:33,383 --> 01:37:36,552
I'm still trying to see what part 
they might have in this,

874
01:37:36,636 --> 01:37:38,429
but I can't really ...

875
01:37:38,721 --> 01:37:41,808
I don't know anything about the conspiracy theories 
or that sort of thing ...

876
01:37:41,891 --> 01:37:44,185
- Okay, well that's the way I want to say it, though

877
01:37:44,268 --> 01:37:46,479
I mean, I want to say ...

878
01:37:48,064 --> 01:37:49,732
Flynn possessed

879
01:37:50,942 --> 01:37:53,402
an undying commitment to 
his family and his friends.

880
01:37:53,486 --> 01:37:55,571
No, Flynn poss-

881
01:37:58,533 --> 01:38:00,410
I need to start again ...

882
01:38:04,914 --> 01:38:07,708
Years passed, and the voices 
asking what really happened

883
01:38:07,792 --> 01:38:09,752
gradually fell silent.

884
01:38:10,461 --> 01:38:13,339
Flynn was gone. 
Not dead, but gone.

885
01:38:13,673 --> 01:38:16,050
We needed to find a new way 
to reach people.

886
01:38:16,134 --> 01:38:18,219
We needed to think like Kevin.

887
01:38:18,428 --> 01:38:20,680
Evolution is the greatest force 
in the material world.

888
01:38:21,931 --> 01:38:24,851
Evolution will provide us 
the next step of intelligent life.

889
01:38:25,226 --> 01:38:28,104
But it will come 
from somewhere unexpected.

890
01:38:30,982 --> 01:38:33,818
And then 
something wonderful happened.

891
01:38:46,789 --> 01:38:48,791
Flynn came back.

892
01:38:50,710 --> 01:38:52,587
Sam Flynn inspired us.

893
01:38:53,129 --> 01:38:54,672
Every year he'd find a new way to

894
01:38:54,756 --> 01:38:57,467
infuriate ENCOM's board with his pranks.

895
01:39:00,386 --> 01:39:03,473
He started doing the work 
that we had almost given up 10 years ago.

896
01:39:08,311 --> 01:39:10,188
We began the search again.

897
01:39:21,282 --> 01:39:23,660
This time, millions of you joined us.

898
01:39:35,630 --> 01:39:37,965
Flynn lives! Flynn lives!

899
01:39:40,051 --> 01:39:44,097
Today, Sam Flynn has brought us 
a little closer to his father

900
01:39:44,180 --> 01:39:45,723
by reclaiming ENCOM.

901
01:39:47,892 --> 01:39:49,936
But these are confusing times.

902
01:39:51,104 --> 01:39:53,064
We may have not found Kevin Flynn,

903
01:39:54,816 --> 01:39:57,402
but Flynn lives in all of us 
who want to believe in him.

904
01:39:59,362 --> 01:40:01,781
This will be my last transmission.

905
01:40:24,470 --> 01:40:25,596
Greetings, program.

906
01:40:27,598 --> 01:40:28,599
What are you doing?

907
01:40:28,683 --> 01:40:31,185
Wiping the hard drive, 
what does it look like I'm doing.

908
01:40:31,269 --> 01:40:33,563
Looks like you are destroying 
ENCOM corporate property

909
01:40:33,646 --> 01:40:34,689
that's what it looks like you're doing.

910
01:40:34,772 --> 01:40:36,858
After the news, 
I didn't know who to trust.

911
01:40:36,941 --> 01:40:38,484
Oh, relax.

912
01:40:38,568 --> 01:40:39,944
There's no need to panic.

913
01:40:40,027 --> 01:40:41,070
That's easy for you to say.

914
01:40:41,154 --> 01:40:43,906
Your house isn't filled with 
20 years of corporate espionage.

915
01:40:43,990 --> 01:40:47,076
Oh? And I'm the one that's still 
employed by ENCOM.

916
01:40:47,160 --> 01:40:49,787
If my board finds out that I've been 
funding your little operation ...

917
01:40:49,871 --> 01:40:52,874
Our little operation, 
Isolated Thinker.

918
01:40:53,499 --> 01:40:54,584
Yeah.

919
01:40:58,337 --> 01:40:59,839
So what do we do now?

920
01:41:00,173 --> 01:41:04,260
Well, I think it's time that we put 
Flynn Lives behind us.

921
01:41:05,053 --> 01:41:07,430
What about the page at the arcade? 
I'm not giving up now.

922
01:41:07,513 --> 01:41:10,808
Flynn may not be back, but I am. 
Sam's made me chairman.

923
01:41:10,892 --> 01:41:13,644
Oh yeah, I saw that on the news. 
Congratulations.

924
01:41:13,728 --> 01:41:15,313
And I want you to join me.

925
01:41:18,566 --> 01:41:21,486
Think of yourself as 
ENCOM's moral compass.

926
01:41:22,695 --> 01:41:25,531
- What about Mackey? 
- He's out. They're all out.

927
01:41:25,615 --> 01:41:26,991
We have our company back.

928
01:41:29,494 --> 01:41:30,995
And that Dillinger kid?

929
01:41:31,412 --> 01:41:34,624
Well, Junior earned his place. He stays.

930
01:41:35,500 --> 01:41:37,126
What about you?

931
01:41:40,463 --> 01:41:42,298
Sign me up, TRON.

932
01:41:42,673 --> 01:41:44,383
Good to have you back, RAM.

933
01:41:49,097 --> 01:41:52,600
One thing. Why do you think 
Flynn gave you the cool nickname?

934
01:41:54,560 --> 01:41:56,270
We are reporting live from ENCOM offices,

935
01:41:56,354 --> 01:41:59,398
where sources indicate that Sam Flynn 
is on his way here

936
01:41:59,482 --> 01:42:00,525
to address the board.

937
01:42:00,608 --> 01:42:03,277
This will be Sam's first public appearance since-

938
01:42:06,614 --> 01:42:08,658
Over here, Sam, one second, over here.

939
01:42:10,535 --> 01:42:11,619
How's it going fellas?

940
01:42:13,663 --> 01:42:14,956
Have a good day.

941
01:42:16,165 --> 01:42:19,585
What do you think your father 
would have said about your actions today?

942
01:42:20,211 --> 01:42:23,673
Sam, do you have any statements 
for the press today?

